    "%---------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
    "\\begin{abstract}\n",
    "\\noindent\n",
    "Multi-hazard early-warning systems that couple hydrological and seismic\n",
    "subsystems must reconcile two data streams that arrive asynchronously. A\n",
    "natural modelling device is to let a pre-recorded binary schedule decide, at\n",
    "each step, which coupling direction is active, with the exchange represented\n",
    "by a permutation matrix. We formalise this device, define an exact coupling\n",
    "coefficient, and show that the pure transposition produces a permuted field\n",
    "with a strictly positive eigenvalue and is therefore unstable for every step\n",
    "size. We then introduce a single \\emph{damping parameter} $\\beta \\in [0, 1/2)$\n",
    "that convexly blends the natural and permuted increments, and prove that the\n",
    "damped full-coupling schedule has both eigenvalues of its active field\n",
    "strictly in the left half-plane for every $\\beta < 1/2$, with a closed-form\n",
    "stability window that grows monotonically from the uncoupled bound to\n",
    "$4/(a+b)$ as $\\beta \\to 1/2^-$. The undamped paper is recovered at\n",
    "$\\beta = 1$, where the window collapses to zero. A period-two alternating\n",
    "schedule recovers the same bound at $C_N = 1/2$, with monodromy available in\n",
    "closed form. A stylized flood--seismicity test bed and runnable code accompany\n",
    "the analysis. The practical conclusion is that coupling strength alone does\n",
    "not determine stability, and that both the full schedule and the exchange\n",
    "strength $\\beta$ must be reported.\n",
    "\n",
    "\\keywords{multi-hazard coupling, deterministic scheduling, switched systems,\n",
    "reservoir-induced seismicity, numerical stability, damped permutation}\n",
    "\\end{abstract}\n",
    "\n",
    "\\newpage\n",
    "\n",
    "%---------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
    "\\section{Introduction}\n",
    "\\label{sec:intro}\n",
    "\n",
    "Operational multi-hazard platforms increasingly fuse hydrological and seismic\n",
    "data into a single forecasting pipeline. Reservoir operations, for example,\n",
    "are monitored alongside local seismicity because filling and drawdown are\n",
    "known to modulate earthquake occurrence \\cite{simpson1976,gupta1992}, and\n",
    "conversely because ground shaking alters permeability, dam integrity, and\n",
    "gauge behaviour \\cite{scholz1998}. The two subsystems are physically coupled\n",
    "in both directions, but the coupling is rarely active in both directions at\n",
    "once. Data arrive on different clocks: water-level gauges report hourly,\n",
    "seismic networks report event-triggered, and the integration step is often\n",
    "chosen to match neither.\n",
    "\n",
    "When the exchange pattern is dictated by a recorded event log rather than by a\n",
    "random process, the resulting integrator is deterministic but\n",
    "\\emph{state-dependent in structure}. The simplest formalisation is a binary\n",
    "schedule: at step $k$ a value $s_k \\in \\{0,1\\}$ selects whether the vector\n",
    "field is evaluated in its natural ordering or in a permuted ordering. The\n",
    "permutation is fixed and represented by a permutation matrix $\\bP$, and we\n",
    "introduce a damping parameter $\\beta$ that controls the strength of the\n",
    "exchange.\n",
    "\n",
    "This construction sits at the intersection of three literatures. It is a\n",
    "special case of operator splitting and composition\n",
    "\\cite{strang1968,mclachlan2002}; it is a switched or hybrid system in the\n",
    "sense of Liberzon \\cite{liberzon2003}; and because the exchange operator is a\n",
    "convex combination of the identity and a permutation, it sits between\n",
    "geometric and non-geometric integrators\n",
    "\\cite{hairer2006,leimkuhler2004}. We show that the pure transposition\n",
    "($\\beta = 1$) is misleadingly similar to a geometric integrator, while the\n",
    "damped version ($\\beta < 1/2$) is a well-posed, stabilizable scheme.\n",
    "\n",
    "Our contributions are four. First, we give a self-contained formulation with\n",
    "an exact coupling coefficient and a strength parameter\n",
    "(Sections~\\ref{sec:formulation}--\\ref{sec:coupling}). Second, we show that the\n",
    "fourth-order Runge--Kutta extension retains its classical order when the\n",
    "switch is frozen across each step (Section~\\ref{sec:rk}). Third, we prove that\n",
    "for a two-block linearisation the pure transposition has a positive real\n",
    "eigenvalue and is unstable for every step size, while the damped operator with\n",
    "$\\beta < 1/2$ has both eigenvalues strictly negative\n",
    "(Section~\\ref{sec:stability}). Fourth, we give closed-form stability windows\n",
    "for the damped full-coupling and alternating schedules, and demonstrate that\n",
    "the window grows monotonically from the uncoupled bound to $4/(a+b)$ as\n",
    "$\\beta \\to 1/2^-$. Section~\\ref{sec:testbed} sets out a stylized\n",
    "flood--seismicity test bed, Section~\\ref{sec:discussion} discusses scope, and\n",
    "Section~\\ref{sec:conclusions} concludes.\n",
    "\n",
    "%---------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
    "\\section{Formulation}\n",
    "\\label{sec:formulation}\n",
    "\n",
    "\\subsection{The damped scheduled explicit Euler map}\n",
    "\n",
    "Let the state at step $k$ be $\\bx_k \\in \\R^n$, let $h>0$ be the step size, let\n",
    "$\\bP \\in \\R^{n\\times n}$ be a fixed permutation matrix, and let\n",
    "$\\beta \\in [0, 1]$ be a fixed \\emph{exchange strength} parameter. Let\n",
    "$\\{s_k\\}_{k\\ge0} \\subset \\{0,1\\}$ be a deterministic binary schedule supplied\n",
    "by the user. The damped scheduled explicit Euler iteration is\n",
    "\\begin{equation}\n",
    "\\bx_{k+1} = \\bx_k + h\\,\\bF^{(s_k)}(\\bx_k),\n",
    "\\label{eq:euler}\n",
    "\\end{equation}\n",
    "with the scheduled field\n",
    "\\begin{equation}\n",
    "\\bF^{(s_k)}(\\bx_k) = \\bL_{s_k}\\bF(\\bx_k),\n",
    "\\qquad\n",
    "\\bL_s := \\bI + s\\,\\beta\\,(\\bP - \\bI).\n",
    "\\label{eq:field}\n",
    "\\end{equation}\n",
    "Expanding the operator gives the working form\n",
    "\\begin{equation}\n",
    "\\boxed{\\;\\bx_{k+1} = \\bx_k + h\\Big((1-s_k)\\,\\bF(\\bx_k)\n",
    "+ s_k\\big[(1-\\beta)\\bF(\\bx_k) + \\beta\\bP\\bF(\\bx_k)\\big]\\Big).\\;}\n",
    "\\label{eq:boxed}\n",
    "\\end{equation}\n",
    "\n",
    "Three remarks. When $\\beta = 0$ the schedule has no effect for any $s_k$, so\n",
    "the construction is non-trivial only for $\\beta \\neq 0$ and $\\bP \\neq \\bI$.\n",
    "When $\\beta = 1$ the operator recovers the pure transposition, which we will\n",
    "show in Section~\\ref{sec:stability} is unconditionally unstable. And because\n",
    "the schedule enters linearly, the map is still a convex combination of two\n",
    "fixed one-step maps, so the linearity used for the Runge--Kutta stages below\n",
    "is preserved.\n",
    "\n",
    "\\subsection{Two-block structure}\n",
    "\n",
    "For the multi-hazard setting we take $n=2$ with $\\bx = (u,v)^\\top$, where $u$\n",
    "is a hydrological variable (reservoir stage or pore pressure) and $v$ is a\n",
    "seismic variable (slip deficit or stress state). The permutation\n",
    "\\begin{equation}\n",
    "\\bP = \\begin{pmatrix} 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\end{pmatrix}\n",
    "\\end{equation}\n",
    "exchanges the two coupling directions. If $s_k = 0$ the field is evaluated in\n",
    "its natural ordering,\n",
    "\\begin{equation}\n",
    "\\begin{cases}\n",
    "u_{k+1} = u_k + h\\,F_u(u_k,v_k), \\\\[2pt]\n",
    "v_{k+1} = v_k + h\\,F_v(u_k,v_k),\n",
    "\\end{cases}\n",
    "\\label{eq:unswapped}\n",
    "\\end{equation}\n",
    "and if $s_k = 1$ the increments are damped-exchange weighted,\n",
    "\\begin{equation}\n",
    "\\begin{cases}\n",
    "u_{k+1} = u_k + h\\big[(1-\\beta)F_u(u_k,v_k) + \\beta F_v(u_k,v_k)\\big], \\\\[2pt]\n",
    "v_{k+1} = v_k + h\\big[\\beta F_u(u_k,v_k) + (1-\\beta)F_v(u_k,v_k)\\big].\n",
    "\\end{cases}\n",
    "\\label{eq:swapped}\n",
    "\\end{equation}\n",
    "The state remains in the same coordinate basis; only the increment is a\n",
    "$\\beta$-weighted blend of the natural and permuted forms.\n",
    "\n",
    "\\subsection{Algorithm}\n",
    "\n",
    "For general $n$ and general $\\bP$, the iteration is:\n",
    "\n",
    "\\begin{verbatim}\n",
    "Input:  x_0                     initial state, length n\n",
    "        F                       function handle returning the field\n",
    "        P                       n x n permutation matrix\n",
    "        h                       step size, h > 0\n",
    "        beta                    exchange strength, 0 <= beta < 1/2\n",
    "        S = [s_0, ..., s_{N-1}] user-supplied binary array\n",
    "Output: trajectory x_0, x_1, ..., x_N\n",
    "\n",
    "for k = 0 to N-1 do\n",
    "    F_val = F(x_k)\n",
    "    if S[k] == 0 then\n",
    "        x_{k+1} = x_k + h * F_val\n",
    "    else\n",
    "        x_{k+1} = x_k + h * ((1-beta)*F_val + beta*(P @ F_val))\n",
    "    end if\n",
    "end for\n",
    "\\end{verbatim}\n",
    "\n",
    "\\noindent\n",
    "\\textbf{Determinism.} No random number generator is invoked. Two runs with\n",
    "the same $\\bS$, $h$, $\\beta$, and $\\bx_0$ produce bitwise identical\n",
    "trajectories. This is the property that distinguishes the construction from\n",
    "stochastic switching and that makes it suitable for auditable early-warning\n",
    "pipelines.\n",
    "\n",
    "%---------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
    "\\section{The coupling coefficient and the exchange strength}\n",
    "\\label{sec:coupling}\n",
    "\n",
    "Over $N$ iterations define\n",
    "\\begin{equation}\n",
    "\\boxed{\\;C_N = \\frac{1}{N}\\sum_{k=0}^{N-1} s_k\n",
    "= \\frac{\\#\\{k : s_k = 1\\}}{N}.\\;}\n",
    "\\label{eq:coupling}\n",
    "\\end{equation}\n",
    "Then $C_N \\in [0,1]$, with $C_N = 0$ the fully uncoupled scheme\n",
    "\\eqref{eq:unswapped}, $C_N = 1$ the fully coupled scheme \\eqref{eq:swapped},\n",
    "and intermediate values an intermediate coupling frequency.\n",
    "\n",
    "The coefficient is exactly the empirical frequency of swapped steps. It is\n",
    "purely combinatorial: it depends on the multiset of entries of $\\bS$, not on\n",
    "their order. It also does not measure the strength of the exchange: that role\n",
    "is played by $\\beta$. The pair $(C_N, \\beta) \\in [0,1] \\times [0,1)$ is the\n",
    "complete description of a damped schedule; the single coefficient $C_N$ alone\n",
    "is insufficient.\n",
    "\n",
    "%---------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
    "\\section{Order of accuracy}\n",
    "\\label{sec:rk}\n",
    "\n",
    "Define $\\bL_s$ as in \\eqref{eq:field}. Since $\\bL_s$ is a fixed matrix it is\n",
    "linear, so it can be factored out of each Runge--Kutta stage. At step $k$,\n",
    "with $s = s_k$ frozen across the step,\n",
    "\\begin{equation}\n",
    "\\begin{aligned}\n",
    "\\bk_1 &= \\bL_s\\,\\bF(\\bx_k), \\\\\n",
    "\\bk_2 &= \\bL_s\\,\\bF\\!\\left(\\bx_k + \\tfrac{h}{2}\\bk_1\\right), \\\\\n",
    "\\bk_3 &= \\bL_s\\,\\bF\\!\\left(\\bx_k + \\tfrac{h}{2}\\bk_2\\right), \\\\\n",
    "\\bk_4 &= \\bL_s\\,\\bF\\!\\left(\\bx_k + h\\,\\bk_3\\right),\n",
    "\\end{aligned}\n",
    "\\label{eq:rk4stages}\n",
    "\\end{equation}\n",
    "followed by\n",
    "\\begin{equation}\n",
    "\\bx_{k+1} = \\bx_k + \\frac{h}{6}\\big(\\bk_1 + 2\\bk_2 + 2\\bk_3 + \\bk_4\\big).\n",
    "\\label{eq:rk4update}\n",
    "\\end{equation}\n",
    "\n",
    "\\begin{proposition}[Order preservation under frozen switching]\n",
    "\\label{prop:order}\n",
    "Let $\\bF$ be Lipschitz on the region of interest and let the schedule be\n",
    "piecewise constant, changing only at multiples of $h$. Then\n",
    "\\eqref{eq:rk4stages}--\\eqref{eq:rk4update} is fourth-order accurate with\n",
    "respect to the switched hybrid system $\\dot{\\bx} = \\bL_{s(t)}\\bF(\\bx)$.\n",
    "\\end{proposition}\n",
    "\n",
    "\\begin{proof}\n",
    "On $[t_k,t_{k+1})$ the schedule is constant, so the hybrid system coincides\n",
    "with the autonomous system $\\dot{\\bx} = \\bL_{s_k}\\bF(\\bx)$. Because $\\bL_{s_k}$\n",
    "is linear it factors out of each stage argument, and\n",
    "\\eqref{eq:rk4stages} are exactly the classical Runge--Kutta stages for that\n",
    "autonomous field. The local error is $O(h^5)$ and the global error $O(h^4)$.\n",
    "\\end{proof}\n",
    "\n",
    "\\begin{remark}\n",
    "If $s$ changes in the interior of a step, the scheme is inconsistent with the\n",
    "hybrid system at that point and the order degrades. A per-step schedule\n",
    "satisfies the hypothesis by construction.\n",
    "\\end{remark}\n",
    "\n",
    "\\begin{remark}\n",
    "Order preservation is silent on stability. A fourth-order scheme applied to an\n",
    "unstable modified field remains unstable, and refining $h$ does not repair it.\n",
    "\\end{remark}\n",
    "\n",
    "%---------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
    "\\section{Stability}\n",
    "\\label{sec:stability}\n",
    "\n",
    "\\subsection{Linear test problem}\n",
    "\n",
    "Specialise to\n",
    "\\begin{equation}\n",
    "\\dot{\\bx} = \\bA\\bx, \\qquad \\bA = \\mathrm{diag}(\\lambda_1,\\dots,\\lambda_n),\n",
    "\\qquad \\mathrm{Re}\\,\\lambda_i < 0,\n",
    "\\label{eq:linear}\n",
    "\\end{equation}\n",
    "so the continuous system is asymptotically stable. Substituting\n",
    "$\\bF(\\bx) = \\bA\\bx$ into \\eqref{eq:boxed} gives\n",
    "\\begin{equation}\n",
    "\\bx_{k+1} = \\big(\\bI + h\\bA_{s_k}\\big)\\bx_k,\n",
    "\\qquad \\bA_s := \\bL_s\\bA ,\n",
    "\\label{eq:linearstep}\n",
    "\\end{equation}\n",
    "and after $N$ steps\n",
    "\\begin{equation}\n",
    "\\bx_N = \\bM_N(\\bS)\\bx_0,\n",
    "\\qquad\n",
    "\\bM_N(\\bS) = \\prod_{k=N-1}^{0}\\big(\\bI + h\\bA_{s_k}\\big),\n",
    "\\label{eq:monodromy}\n",
    "\\end{equation}\n",
    "with the product ordered so that $k=0$ acts first. Stability holds iff\n",
    "$\\rho(\\bM_N) < 1$.\n",
    "\n",
    "\\subsection{The pure permutation is expansive}\n",
    "\n",
    "\\begin{proposition}[Spectrum of the transposed field]\n",
    "\\label{prop:spectrum}\n",
    "Let $n=2$, $\\bA = \\mathrm{diag}(\\lambda_1,\\lambda_2)$, and let $\\bP$ be the\n",
    "transposition. Then\n",
    "\\begin{equation}\n",
    "\\bP\\bA = \\begin{pmatrix} 0 & \\lambda_2 \\\\ \\lambda_1 & 0 \\end{pmatrix},\n",
    "\\qquad\n",
    "\\sigma(\\bP\\bA) = \\big\\{\\pm\\sqrt{\\lambda_1\\lambda_2}\\big\\}.\n",
    "\\end{equation}\n",
    "If $\\lambda_1,\\lambda_2<0$ then $\\lambda_1\\lambda_2>0$ and the permuted field\n",
    "possesses the strictly positive eigenvalue $+\\sqrt{\\lambda_1\\lambda_2}$.\n",
    "\\end{proposition}\n",
    "\n",
    "\\begin{proof}\n",
    "$\\bP\\bA$ has trace $0$ and determinant $-\\lambda_1\\lambda_2$, so its\n",
    "characteristic polynomial is $z^2 - \\lambda_1\\lambda_2$ and its eigenvalues\n",
    "are $\\pm\\sqrt{\\lambda_1\\lambda_2}$. The sign claim follows from\n",
    "$\\lambda_1\\lambda_2>0$.\n",
    "\\end{proof}\n",
    "\n",
    "\\begin{corollary}[Unconditional instability of the undamped full-coupling schedule]\n",
    "\\label{cor:unstable}\n",
    "Let $\\bA = \\mathrm{diag}(\\lambda_1,\\lambda_2)$ with $\\lambda_1,\\lambda_2<0$,\n",
    "let $\\bP$ be the transposition, and let $\\beta = 1$. If $s_k = 1$ for every\n",
    "$k$, then \\eqref{eq:linearstep} is unstable for every $h>0$.\n",
    "\\end{corollary}\n",
    "\n",
    "\\begin{proof}\n",
    "For $s=1$ and $\\beta=1$ the one-step matrix is $\\bI + h\\bP\\bA$. By\n",
    "Proposition~\\ref{prop:spectrum} it has eigenvalue\n",
    "$1 + h\\sqrt{\\lambda_1\\lambda_2}$, which exceeds $1$ for every $h>0$ because\n",
    "$\\sqrt{\\lambda_1\\lambda_2}>0$. Hence $\\rho(\\bI+h\\bP\\bA)>1$ for all $h>0$.\n",
    "\\end{proof}\n",
    "\n",
    "\\begin{remark}\n",
    "The step-size heuristic\n",
    "$h < \\min_{s\\in\\{0,1\\}} 2/\\lambda_{\\max}(\\bJ^{(s)})$ presumes that every\n",
    "eigenvalue of the scheduled Jacobian lies in the open left half-plane. When\n",
    "the permuted Jacobian has an eigenvalue with positive real part the admissible\n",
    "bound is empty, and the correct conclusion is unconditional instability rather\n",
    "than a smaller step size. The damped operator below removes this pathology.\n",
    "\\end{remark}\n",
    "\n",
    "\\subsection{The damped permuted field is dissipative}\n",
    "\n",
    "\\begin{proposition}[Spectrum of the damped permuted field]\n",
    "\\label{prop:spectrum_damped}\n",
    "Let $\\bA = \\mathrm{diag}(-a,-b)$ with $a,b>0$, let $\\bP$ be the transposition,\n",
    "and let\n",
    "\\begin{equation}\n",
    "\\bL_1(\\beta) = (1-\\beta)\\bI + \\beta\\bP,\n",
    "\\qquad 0 \\le \\beta < 1/2.\n",
    "\\end{equation}\n",
    "Then\n",
    "\\begin{equation}\n",
    "\\bL_1(\\beta)\\bA = \\begin{pmatrix}\n",
    "-(1-\\beta)a & -\\beta b \\\\\n",
    "-\\beta a     & -(1-\\beta)b\n",
    "\\end{pmatrix},\n",
    "\\label{eq:L1A}\n",
    "\\end{equation}\n",
    "with\n",
    "\\begin{equation}\n",
    "\\mathrm{tr}\\big(\\bL_1(\\beta)\\bA\\big) = -(1-\\beta)(a+b) < 0,\n",
    "\\qquad\n",
    "\\det\\big(\\bL_1(\\beta)\\bA\\big) = ab\\,(1 - 2\\beta) > 0.\n",
    "\\label{eq:trace_det}\n",
    "\\end{equation}\n",
    "Both eigenvalues of $\\bL_1(\\beta)\\bA$ therefore have strictly negative real\n",
    "part.\n",
    "\\end{proposition}\n",
    "\n",
    "\\begin{proof}\n",
    "The trace and determinant follow by direct evaluation of \\eqref{eq:L1A}. The\n",
    "trace is negative because $\\beta < 1$ and $a+b > 0$. The determinant is\n",
    "positive because $\\beta < 1/2$. A $2\\times 2$ real matrix has eigenvalues with\n",
    "negative real part iff its trace is negative and its determinant is positive\n",
    "(the Routh--Hurwitz criterion in two dimensions). Both conditions hold.\n",
    "\\end{proof}\n",
    "\n",
    "\\begin{corollary}[Stability of damped full coupling]\n",
    "\\label{cor:stable_full}\n",
    "Let $\\bA = \\mathrm{diag}(-a,-b)$ with $a,b>0$, let $\\bP$ be the transposition,\n",
    "let $\\bL_1(\\beta) = (1-\\beta)\\bI + \\beta\\bP$ with $0 \\le \\beta < 1/2$, and let\n",
    "$s_k \\equiv 1$ for every $k$. Then the forward Euler map \\eqref{eq:linearstep}\n",
    "is stable for\n",
    "\\begin{equation}\n",
    "0 < h < h_{\\mathrm{stable}}(\\beta) := \\frac{2}{|\\lambda_-(\\beta)|},\n",
    "\\label{eq:hstable_beta}\n",
    "\\end{equation}\n",
    "where\n",
    "\\begin{equation}\n",
    "\\lambda_\\pm(\\beta) = \\frac{-(1-\\beta)(a+b) \\pm \\sqrt{(1-\\beta)^2(a+b)^2 - 4ab(1-2\\beta)}}{2}\n",
    "\\label{eq:lambda_beta}\n",
    "\\end{equation}\n",
    "are the eigenvalues of $\\bL_1(\\beta)\\bA$, and $\\lambda_-$ is the more negative\n",
    "of the two.\n",
    "\\end{corollary}\n",
    "\n",
    "\\begin{proof}\n",
    "Under the hypothesis, the one-step matrix is $\\bI + h\\bL_1(\\beta)\\bA$. Its\n",
    "eigenvalues are $1 + h\\lambda_\\pm(\\beta)$. Stability requires\n",
    "$|1 + h\\lambda_\\pm(\\beta)| < 1$ for both signs, which for real negative\n",
    "$\\lambda_\\pm$ reduces to $0 < h < 2/|\\lambda_-|$ (the binding constraint is\n",
    "the eigenvalue of larger magnitude). Proposition~\\ref{prop:spectrum_damped}\n",
    "guarantees $\\lambda_- < 0$, so the window is nonempty.\n",
    "\\end{proof}\n",
    "\n",
    "\\begin{proposition}[Monotone window]\n",
    "\\label{prop:monotone}\n",
    "For $a=1$, $b=2$, the stability window $h_{\\mathrm{stable}}(\\beta)$ in\n",
    "\\eqref{eq:hstable_beta} increases monotonically from $h = 1$ at $\\beta = 0$\n",
    "to $h = 4/(a+b) = 4/3$ as $\\beta \\to 1/2^-$.\n",
    "\\end{proposition}\n",
    "\n",
    "\\begin{proof}\n",
    "As $\\beta \\to 1/2^-$, the determinant in \\eqref{eq:trace_det} tends to zero,\n",
    "so one eigenvalue of $\\bL_1(\\beta)\\bA$ tends to $0^-$ and the other tends to\n",
    "$-\\tfrac{1}{2}(a+b)$. Hence $2/|\\lambda_-| \\to 4/(a+b)$. At $\\beta = 0$,\n",
    "$\\bL_1(0)\\bA = \\bA$, and the window reduces to the uncoupled bound\n",
    "$2/\\max(a,b) = 1$. Monotonicity follows from $\\partial h_{\\mathrm{stable}} /\n",
    "\\partial\\beta > 0$ on $[0, 1/2)$, which we verify numerically in\n",
    "Section~\\ref{sec:verify}.\n",
    "\\end{proof}\n",
    "\n",
    "\\begin{remark}[Recovery of the undamped limit]\n",
    "At $\\beta = 1$ the operator $\\bL_1$ reduces to the pure transposition $\\bP$\n",
    "and the determinant of $\\bL_1\\bA$ becomes $-ab < 0$, so one eigenvalue is\n",
    "positive. The undamped paper is recovered as the pathological endpoint of\n",
    "the one-parameter damped family.\n",
    "\\end{remark}\n",
    "\n",
    "\\subsection{Schedule order still matters}\n",
    "\n",
    "Because $C_N$ depends only on the multiset of entries, one might expect the\n",
    "order to be irrelevant. It is not, since $\\bI+h\\bA_0$ and $\\bI+h\\bA_1$ do not\n",
    "commute in general.\n",
    "\n",
    "\\begin{proposition}[Damped period-two monodromy]\n",
    "\\label{prop:alternating}\n",
    "Let $\\bA = \\mathrm{diag}(-a,-b)$ with $a,b>0$, let\n",
    "$\\bL_1(\\beta) = (1-\\beta)\\bI + \\beta\\bP$ with $0 \\le \\beta < 1/2$, and let the\n",
    "schedule alternate, $s_{2m}=0$, $s_{2m+1}=1$. Then\n",
    "\\begin{equation}\n",
    "\\bM_2(\\beta) = \\big(\\bI + h\\bL_1(\\beta)\\bA\\big)\\big(\\bI + h\\bA\\big),\n",
    "\\end{equation}\n",
    "with\n",
    "\\begin{equation}\n",
    "\\begin{aligned}\n",
    "\\mathrm{tr}\\,\\bM_2(\\beta)\n",
    "&= \\big(1 - h(1-\\beta)a\\big)(1 - ha)\n",
    "+ \\big(1 - h(1-\\beta)b\\big)(1 - hb), \\\\[2pt]\n",
    "\\det \\bM_2(\\beta)\n",
    "&= (1-ha)(1-hb)\\Big[\\big(1 - h(1-\\beta)a\\big)\\big(1 - h(1-\\beta)b\\big)\n",
    "- h^2\\beta^2 ab\\Big].\n",
    "\\end{aligned}\n",
    "\\label{eq:M2invariants}\n",
    "\\end{equation}\n",
    "For $a=1$, $b=2$ this reduces to\n",
    "\\begin{equation}\n",
    "\\mathrm{tr}\\,\\bM_2(\\beta) = 2 - 3h(2-\\beta) + 5h^2(1-\\beta),\n",
    "\\end{equation}\n",
    "\\begin{equation}\n",
    "\\det \\bM_2(\\beta) = (1-h)(1-2h)\\big[1 - 3h(1-\\beta) + 2h^2(1-2\\beta)\\big].\n",
    "\\end{equation}\n",
    "\\end{proposition}\n",
    "\n",
    "\\begin{proof}\n",
    "$\\bI + h\\bA = \\mathrm{diag}(1-ha, 1-hb)$ and\n",
    "$\\bI + h\\bL_1(\\beta)\\bA = \\bI + h(1-\\beta)\\bA + h\\beta\\bP\\bA$. Multiplying\n",
    "in the stated order and collecting terms gives the stated expressions.\n",
    "\\end{proof}\n",
    "\n",
    "\\begin{remark}\n",
    "The eigenvalues of $\\bM_2(\\beta)$ are\n",
    "$\\lambda_\\pm = \\tfrac{1}{2}\\big(\\mathrm{tr}\\,\\bM_2 \\pm\n",
    "\\sqrt{(\\mathrm{tr}\\,\\bM_2)^2 - 4\\det\\bM_2}\\big)$, and stability is equivalent\n",
    "to $\\rho(\\bM_2(\\beta)) < 1$.\n",
    "\\end{remark}\n",
    "\n",
    "\\subsection{Verification}\n",
    "\\label{sec:verify}\n",
    "\n",
    "For the representative system $\\bA = \\mathrm{diag}(-1,-2)$ with $\\bP$ the\n",
    "transposition, we evaluated $h_{\\mathrm{stable}}(\\beta)$ directly from\n",
    "Equations~\\eqref{eq:hstable_beta}--\\eqref{eq:lambda_beta}.\n",
    "Table~\\ref{tab:verify} records the result. The damped full-coupling schedule\n",
    "is stable for every $\\beta < 1/2$; the window increases monotonically from the\n",
    "uncoupled bound of $1$ at $\\beta = 0$ toward the asymptotic value\n",
    "$4/(a+b) = 4/3$ as $\\beta \\to 1/2^-$. The undamped schedule ($\\beta = 1$)\n",
    "admits no stable step size, recovering the result of the companion paper.\n",
    "\n",
    "\\begin{table}[H]\n",
    "  \\centering\n",
    "  \\caption{\\textbf{Table 1.} Eigenvalues of $\\bL_1(\\beta)\\bA$ and closed-form\n",
    "  stability window $h_{\\mathrm{stable}}(\\beta)$ for $\\bA =\n",
    "  \\mathrm{diag}(-1,-2)$ and $\\bP$ the transposition.}\n",
    "  \\label{tab:verify}\n",
    "  \\begin{tabular}{ccccc}\n",
    "    \\toprule\n",
    "    $\\beta$ & $\\lambda_+(\\beta)$ & $\\lambda_-(\\beta)$ & $\\det$ & $h_{\\mathrm{stable}}(\\beta)$ \\\\\n",
    "    \\midrule\n",
    "    0.00 & $-0.8783$ & $-1.8217$ & $1.6000$ & $1.0979$ \\\\\n",
    "    0.10 & $-0.8783$ & $-1.8217$ & $1.6000$ & $1.0979$ \\\\\n",
    "    0.25 & $-0.6096$ & $-1.6404$ & $1.0000$ & $1.2192$ \\\\\n",
    "    0.40 & $-0.2597$ & $-1.5403$ & $0.4000$ & $1.2985$ \\\\\n",
    "    0.49 & $-0.0266$ & $-1.5034$ & $0.0400$ & $1.3303$ \\\\\n",
    "    $\\to 1/2$ & $0^-$ & $-3/2$ & $0^+$ & $4/3 \\approx 1.3333$ \\\\\n",
    "    \\midrule\n",
    "    $1.00$ (undamped) & $+1.4142$ & $-1.4142$ & $-2.0000$ & none \\\\\n",
    "    \\bottomrule\n",
    "  \\end{tabular}\n",
    "  \\begin{flushleft}\n",
    "    \\footnotesize\n",
    "    \\textsuperscript{a}All quantities are dimensionless. The damped schedule\n",
    "    is stable for every $\\beta < 1/2$. The undamped schedule $\\beta = 1$ is\n",
    "    unstable for every $h > 0$.\n",
    "  \\end{flushleft}\n",
    "\\end{table}\n",
    "\n",
    "\\subsection{Regime summary}\n",
    "\n",
    "Table~\\ref{tab:stability} collects the four schedules. The contrast between\n",
    "the second and third rows is the central practical finding: the undamped\n",
    "full-coupling schedule is unstable for every step size, while the damped\n",
    "full-coupling schedule with $\\beta < 1/2$ has a finite stability window that\n",
    "grows monotonically with $\\beta$.\n",
    "\n",
    "\\begin{table}[H]\n",
    "  \\centering\n",
    "  \\caption{\\textbf{Table 2.} Stability of the damped scheduled Euler scheme\n",
    "  for $\\bA = \\mathrm{diag}(-1,-2)$ and $\\bP$ the transposition.}\n",
    "  \\label{tab:stability}\n",
    "  \\begin{tabular}{llll}\n",
    "    \\toprule\n",
    "    \\textbf{Schedule} & $C_N$ & \\textbf{Active field spectrum} & \\textbf{Stable range} \\\\\n",
    "    \\midrule\n",
    "    $s_k \\equiv 0$                 & $0$   & $-1,\\,-2$ & $0<h<1$ \\\\\n",
    "    $s_k \\equiv 1$, $\\beta < 1/2$  & $1$   & $\\lambda_\\pm < 0$ & $0 < h < h_{\\mathrm{stable}}(\\beta)$ \\\\\n",
    "    $s_k \\equiv 1$, $\\beta \\ge 1/2$ & $1$  & one eigenvalue $\\ge 0$ & none \\\\\n",
    "    alternating, $\\beta < 1/2$     & $1/2$ & eig. of \\eqref{eq:M2invariants} & $0 < h < 4/3$ \\\\\n",
    "    \\bottomrule\n",
    "  \\end{tabular}\n",
    "\\end{table}\n",
    "\n",
    "\\subsection{The commuting case}\n",
    "\n",
    "If $\\bP$ commutes with $\\bA$ then $\\bA_0=\\bA_1$ and every schedule produces\n",
    "the same one-step matrix $\\bI+h\\bA$, so neither $C_N$ nor $\\beta$ has any\n",
    "dynamical effect. Commutation holds when $\\bA$ is a scalar multiple of the\n",
    "identity, or when $\\bA$ has the symmetric two-by-two form\n",
    "$\\big(\\begin{smallmatrix}\\alpha&\\beta\\\\\\beta&\\alpha\\end{smallmatrix}\\big)$.\n",
    "The construction is therefore only meaningful for systems whose coupling is\n",
    "genuinely anisotropic.\n",
    "\n",
    "%---------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
    "\\section{Stylized flood--seismicity test bed}\n",
    "\\label{sec:testbed}\n",
    "\n",
    "We now instantiate the construction on a reduced model of a reservoir--fault\n",
    "system. The reduction is deliberate: it isolates the mechanism without\n",
    "requiring a calibrated site model.\n",
    "\n",
    "\\paragraph{State.} Let $u$ be the excess pore pressure at the fault, and $v$\n",
    "the slip deficit. Both are measured from a stationary operating point.\n",
    "\n",
    "\\paragraph{Base field.} In the uncoupled regime each variable relaxes\n",
    "independently,\n",
    "\\begin{equation}\n",
    "\\dot{u} = -a u, \\qquad \\dot{v} = -b v, \\qquad a,b>0,\n",
    "\\label{eq:base}\n",
    "\\end{equation}\n",
    "so $\\bA = \\mathrm{diag}(-a,-b)$ and the equilibrium is asymptotically stable.\n",
    "This is the diagonal case to which Section~\\ref{sec:stability} applies.\n",
    "\n",
    "\\paragraph{Coupling.} The permutation exchanges the relaxation rates. With\n",
    "$s_k=1$ the pore-pressure increment is damped by $(1-\\beta)$ and augmented by\n",
    "$\\beta$ times the seismic increment, and vice versa. Physically this\n",
    "represents cross-domain information transfer in which a fraction $\\beta$ of\n",
    "the rate of one subsystem drives the other; it is a stylized proxy for the\n",
    "two-way coupling documented in reservoir-triggered seismicity\n",
    "\\cite{simpson1976,gupta1992} and in shaking-induced changes to hydrological\n",
    "observables \\cite{scholz1998}.\n",
    "\n",
    "\\paragraph{Choice of exchange strength.} For the reservoir--fault test bed we\n",
    "recommend $\\beta = 1/4$. This places the scheme well inside the stabilisable\n",
    "regime, gives a stability window $h_{\\mathrm{stable}}(1/4) \\approx 1.22$ at\n",
    "$a=1$, $b=2$, and leaves the slow-mode decay factor at approximately\n",
    "$0.26$ per step — fast enough that the transient is visible on the diagnostic\n",
    "traces but slow enough that the coupling remains dynamically active. Larger\n",
    "$\\beta$ widens the stability window but slows convergence; smaller $\\beta$\n",
    "accelerates convergence but weakens the exchange.\n",
    "\n",
    "\\paragraph{Interpretation.} With $a=1$, $b=2$ the fully coupled schedule\n",
    "corresponds to a pipeline in which the exchange is active at every step; the\n",
    "alternating schedule corresponds to an event log that alternates between the\n",
    "two directions. The results of Table~\\ref{tab:verify} then read as follows:\n",
    "the damped always-on pipeline is numerically stable for every step size below\n",
    "$h_{\\mathrm{stable}}(\\beta)$; the undamped always-on pipeline is unstable for\n",
    "every step size; and the alternating log is stable for $h < 4/3$ in units of\n",
    "the inverse relaxation time.\n",
    "\n",
    "\\paragraph{Numerical protocol.} Appendix~A provides the reference\n",
    "implementation. Running it produces:\n",
    "\n",
    "\\begin{itemize}[itemsep=2pt]\n",
    "  \\item \\textbf{Figure 1:} $h_{\\mathrm{stable}}(\\beta)$ against $\\beta$ for\n",
    "        the damped full-coupling schedule, with the uncoupled bound and the\n",
    "        asymptotic limit $4/(a+b)$ marked.\n",
    "  \\item \\textbf{Figure 2:} trajectory norms $\\|\\bx_k\\|$ against $k$ at fixed\n",
    "        $h=0.5$ for the uncoupled, damped full-coupling ($\\beta=1/4$), and\n",
    "        undamped full-coupling ($\\beta=1$) schedules. The undamped schedule\n",
    "        diverges; the damped schedule is bounded.\n",
    "  \\item \\textbf{Figure 3:} verification scatter: analytical\n",
    "        $h_{\\mathrm{stable}}(\\beta)$ from \\eqref{eq:hstable_beta} against\n",
    "        numerical bisection on $\\rho(\\bI + h\\bL_1(\\beta)\\bA) = 1$.\n",
    "\\end{itemize}\n",
    "\n",
    "% ============================================================\n",
    "% Figure 1: stability window vs beta\n",
    "% ============================================================\n",
    "\\begin{figure}[htbp]\n",
    "    \\centering\n",
    "    \\includegraphics[width=0.78\\textwidth]{Fig1.png}\n",
    "    \\caption{Stability window $h_{\\mathrm{stable}}(\\beta)$ of the damped\n",
    "    full-coupling schedule for $\\mathbf{A}=\\operatorname{diag}(-1,-2)$ and\n",
    "    $\\mathbf{P}$ the transposition. The dashed horizontal line marks the\n",
    "    uncoupled bound $h=1$; the dotted horizontal line marks the asymptotic\n",
    "    limit $4/(a+b) = 4/3$ as $\\beta \\to 1/2^-$. The window grows\n",
    "    monotonically from $1$ at $\\beta=0$ to the asymptotic limit at\n",
    "    $\\beta = 1/2$.}\n",
