    "    \\centering\n",
    "    \\includegraphics[width=0.78\\textwidth]{Fig3.png}\n",
    "    \\caption{Verification scatter: the analytical stability window\n",
    "    $h_{\\mathrm{stable}}(\\beta)$ from \\eqref{eq:hstable_beta} (red curve)\n",
    "    against the boundary located by direct numerical bisection on the\n",
    "    spectral radius $\\rho(\\bI + h\\bL_1(\\beta)\\bA) = 1$ (blue dots). The\n",
    "    dashed horizontal line marks the uncoupled bound $h = 1$. The two agree\n",
    "    to numerical precision across the full range $0 \\le \\beta < 1/2$.}\n",
    "    \\label{fig:verification}\n",
    "\\end{figure}\n",
    "\n",
    "%---------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
    "\\section{Discussion}\n",
    "\\label{sec:discussion}\n",
    "\n",
    "\\paragraph{Merits.} The construction is exactly deterministic, trivially\n",
    "reproducible from the tuple $(\\bx_0,\\bF,\\bP,h,\\beta,\\bS)$, and modular:\n",
    "because $\\bL_s$ is linear it can be inserted at any stage of any explicit\n",
    "Runge--Kutta method without altering the algebraic structure, as\n",
    "Proposition~\\ref{prop:order} records.\n",
    "\n",
    "\\paragraph{Where the naive analysis fails.} The heuristic that stability\n",
    "follows from $h<2/\\lambda_{\\max}(\\bJ^{(s)})$ is valid only when every\n",
    "eigenvalue of the scheduled Jacobian has negative real part. The pure\n",
    "permuted field violates that premise, and Corollary~\\ref{cor:unstable} shows\n",
    "that when it does no step size stabilises the undamped schedule. The damped\n",
    "operator of Proposition~\\ref{prop:spectrum_damped} restores the premise for\n",
    "every $\\beta < 1/2$.\n",
    "\n",
    "\\paragraph{Coupling coefficient is not enough.} Because $C_N$ depends only on\n",
    "the multiset of schedule entries it cannot distinguish a stable schedule from\n",
    "an unstable one, as the comparison of $\\beta=1/4$ and $\\beta=1$ in\n",
    "Table~\\ref{tab:stability} shows. The pair $(C_N, \\beta)$ is the complete\n",
    "description. Studies that characterise a simulation only by its coupling\n",
    "coefficient are under-determined.\n",
    "\n",
    "\\paragraph{Relation to geometric integration.} The pure permutation is\n",
    "orthogonal, which invites the expectation that the scheme inherits a geometric\n",
    "property from the base method. It does not: $\\bP\\bA$ is generally not similar\n",
    "to $\\bA$ through an orthogonal transformation and its spectrum can differ, as\n",
    "Proposition~\\ref{prop:spectrum} shows. The damped operator is not orthogonal\n",
    "either, but it is dissipative in the sense of Proposition~\\ref{prop:spectrum_damped}.\n",
    "The construction is a switched hybrid integrator, not a geometric one.\n",
    "\n",
    "\\paragraph{Scope and limitations.} The analysis is restricted to linear\n",
    "autonomous test problems and to the transposition in two dimensions. Extension\n",
    "to general cycles is straightforward in principle: transposing coordinates $i$\n",
    "and $j$ within a diagonal matrix produces eigenvalues\n",
    "$\\pm\\sqrt{\\lambda_i\\lambda_j}$ together with the unpermuted $\\lambda_k$ for\n",
    "$k\\notin\\{i,j\\}$, and longer cycles factor into two-by-two blocks. The\n",
    "damping analysis extends to general $\\bP$ because the argument only uses the\n",
    "trace and determinant of the active field. Nonlinear fields require\n",
    "linearisation about a trajectory, after which the same spectral criteria\n",
    "apply locally.\n",
    "\n",
    "\\paragraph{Open question.} The damped full-coupling schedule with\n",
    "$\\beta < 1/2$ achieves a finite stability window for the two-block\n",
    "linearisation. Whether the same remedy extends to higher-dimensional\n",
    "permutations, or whether a longer schedule period can deliver $C_N$ closer to\n",
    "$1$ while retaining a finite window, is a natural question that we do not\n",
    "settle here; both are amenable to the same monodromy calculation at\n",
    "dimension $n$ and period three and above.\n",
    "\n",
    "%---------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
    "\\section{Conclusions}\n",
    "\\label{sec:conclusions}\n",
    "\n",
    "We formalised a deterministic damped permutation-scheduled family of explicit\n",
    "integrators and analysed its coupling, order, and stability. The main findings\n",
    "are: (i) the schedule average $C_N$ is an exact coupling coefficient in\n",
    "$[0,1]$, and the pair $(C_N, \\beta)$ is the complete schedule description;\n",
    "(ii) with the switch frozen across each step the fourth-order Runge--Kutta\n",
    "variant retains classical order; (iii) for the two-block linearisation the\n",
    "undamped permuted field has eigenvalues $\\pm\\sqrt{\\lambda_1\\lambda_2}$ and is\n",
    "unstable for every $h>0$, while the damped operator\n",
    "$\\bL_1(\\beta) = (1-\\beta)\\bI + \\beta\\bP$ with $\\beta < 1/2$ has both\n",
    "eigenvalues strictly negative and a finite stability window\n",
    "$h_{\\mathrm{stable}}(\\beta) = 2/|\\lambda_-(\\beta)|$; and (iv) the window grows\n",
    "monotonically from the uncoupled bound to the asymptotic limit $4/(a+b)$ as\n",
    "$\\beta \\to 1/2^-$. The practical recommendation is that any study using a\n",
    "scheduled permutation integrator should report the full binary schedule, the\n",
    "exchange strength $\\beta$, and should verify stability against the spectral\n",
    "radius of the active field rather than against a per-step step-size rule.\n",
    "\n",
